-- Demandé par Tom le 03/11/2026 : version anglaise de l'hommage à Jesús de Miguel.
UPDATE "articles" SET "en_title" = 'Jesús de Miguel: Passe D''s tribute', "en_dek" = '⭐ Jesús de Miguel, CD Tenerife striker, passed away on the morning of Tuesday 3 November. He was 30. Spanish football mourns one of its own, and Passe D bows its head. 🕊️', "en_body_html" = '<p>Some news you never want to write. This is one of them.</p><h2>A match that turned into a tragedy</h2><p>On Monday, at the Heliodoro Rodríguez López stadium, CD Tenerife hosted FC Andorra in LaLiga 2. In the closing minutes, a long ball drops in behind the defence. ⭐ Jesús de Miguel races after it, and the Andorra goalkeeper, ⭐ Jesús Owono, comes out of his box to clear. The collision is violent, in the kind of duel football sees thousands of times every weekend.</p><p>Jesús de Miguel stays down. He has gone into cardiac arrest. Medical staff treat him on the pitch, then he is rushed to the Nuestra Señora de Candelaria University Hospital. He is resuscitated and admitted to intensive care. The match is abandoned in the 108th minute. Nobody had their mind on football any more.</p><p>During the night, the club gives an update: his condition is stable but serious. Then, early in the morning, his neurological condition deteriorates. On Tuesday at 8 a.m., CD Tenerife announces his death. In its statement, the club says it is broken with grief and unable to believe this is real.</p><h2>A player who had won hearts</h2><p>Born in 1996, Jesús de Miguel built his career step by step, far from the spotlight. From Internacional de Madrid to Fuenlabrada, by way of Navalcarnero, Unionistas de Salamanca and Castellón, he climbed the ladder with patience. After joining Tenerife in 2025, he quickly won over the Canary Islands supporters.</p><p>A hard worker''s journey, the kind of player who truly loves this game.</p><h2>Football, struck once again</h2><p>This tragedy brings back others that have marked our sport forever:</p><ul><li>⭐ Marc-Vivien Foé, the Cameroonian midfielder, collapsed on the pitch at Gerland, in Lyon, in 2003, during the Confederations Cup. He did not survive.</li><li>⭐ Antonio Puerta, a Sevilla player, collapsed during a match in 2007. He died a few days later, aged 22.</li><li>⭐ Petr Čech, the Chelsea goalkeeper, suffered a serious head injury after a collision with an opponent in 2006. He recovered, but played the rest of his career wearing a helmet.</li><li>⭐ Fabrice Muamba in 2012 and ⭐ Christian Eriksen at Euro 2021 suffered cardiac arrests on the pitch. They were saved thanks to the speed of the medical response.</li></ul><p>Each time, the football world freezes. And each time, the same question comes back: how can we better protect those who make us dream?</p><h2>A unanimous tribute</h2><p>FC Andorra sent its most sincere condolences to the family, heartbroken. FC Barcelona and many other clubs also expressed their sadness. Spanish football is in mourning.</p><p>Our thoughts also go to ⭐ Jesús Owono, caught up through no fault of his own in this terrible accident. No player ever steps onto a pitch for this to happen.</p><h2>Our thoughts are with his family</h2><p>To Jesús''s family, his loved ones, his teammates, CD Tenerife and all the Canary Islands supporters: we know these words may never reach you. But we want you to know that everyone at Passe D is with you. We share your grief and send you our deepest condolences.</p><p><strong>Descansa en paz, Jesús.</strong> 🕊️</p><p>— Passe D</p>', "en_published" = true
WHERE "slug" = 'jesus-de-miguel-l-hommage-de-passe-d' AND "en_title" = '';
